# Student add permissions (non-negotiable)

## Product rule

**Every school member role** — `owner`, `department_head`, and `teacher` — **may add students** on every surface that adds pupils:

- Class Students panel (`POST /api/tenants/.../students`)
- School Active Students list (`POST /api/tenants/.../school-students`)
- Locate / enroll from active list into a class (`POST .../school-students/.../enrollments`) when the actor can use that class

Helpers: `canAddStudentsToClass`, `canUseSchoolRoster` in `app/src/lib/auth/`. Do **not** reintroduce owner/DH-only gates on **add**.

Archive / remove from active list / move between classes may stay lead-only (`canManageSchoolRoster`) unless the maintainer says otherwise.

## Do not change without asking

**Never** tighten, loosen, or redesign **role / access permissions** (who may add students, edit classes, timetable, billing, etc.) without **explicit maintainer approval in that chat first**.

Fixing a bug that blocks an allowed role from doing something they already should do is fine. Inventing a new restriction is not.

